        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7d4e6ef4-a614-51c2-af8d-acd145a0582c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Klitgaarden, Skagen, Jutland\n- People: Ulrik Plesner, King Christian X, Queen Alexandrine, Alexandrine of Mecklenburg-Schwerin\n- Roles: Danish royal family, Queen of Denmark, Queen of Iceland\n\nFacts:\n- Queen Alexandrine of Mecklenburg-Schwerin was born on 24 December 1879 and died on 28 December 1952.\n- Queen Alexandrine was Queen of Denmark as the spouse of King Christian X.\n- Queen Alexandrine also held the title of Queen of Iceland.\n- Klitgaarden is a former summer residence of the Danish royal family located just south of Skagen on the northern tip of Jutland.\n- Ulrik Plesner designed the two-story house Klitgaarden for King Christian X and Queen Alexandrine.\n- Klitgaarden was completed in 1914.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "08ac9c0d-4eb8-53a1-bea2-1702a0397d45",
        "text": "Klitgaarden (lit.\"The Dune House\") is a former summer residence of the Danish royal family situated just south of Skagen on the northern tip of Jutland; the two-story house was designed by Ulrik Plesner, and completed in 1914, for King Christian X and Queen Alexandrine, Alexandrine of Mecklenburg-Schwerin (24 December 1879 – 28 December 1952) was Queen of Denmark as the spouse of King Christian X, she also held the title of Queen of Iceland.",
